    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nvim.lsp.util.open_floating_preview() hardcodes conceallevel=2 when stylizing Markdown hover contents. This causes the rendered contents and floating-window height to change when the cursor moves over concealed Markdown syntax, resulting in visually distracting layout jumps.\n\nMarkdown highlighting and Markdown conceal are separate presentation choices. The latter should not be an unconditional side effect of enabling hover stylization.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nAdd a `conceallevel` or `markdown_conceallevel` option in `vim.lsp.util.open_floating_preview.Opts`, the float window's conceallevel can be customed then.",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "enhancing `open_floating_preview` is out of scope. \n\nI think we should add new `style` kinds to `nvim_open_win`, which provide \"recipes\" for creating common configurations of windows/popups. That will make `nvim_open_win` easy to use for various common use-cases, and eliminates `open_floating_preview` \n\nthat would also resolve  https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/25514",
            "created_at": "2026-09-01T15:13:54Z",
